Done. The book catalogue is implemented and verified.

## What I added

**`src/main/java/com/example/catalog/Book.java`** — the `Book` aggregate record (the only domain code; Prefab generates the controller, service, repository, request/response DTOs and the DB migration):

```java
@Aggregate
@GetById
public record Book(
        @Id Reference<Book> id,
        @Version long version,
        String title,
        String author,
        String isbn,
        Integer publicationYear
) {
    @Create
    public Book(
            @NotBlank @Size(max = 200) String title,
            @NotBlank String author,
            @NotBlank String isbn,
            @NotNull Integer publicationYear
    ) {
        this(Reference.create(), 0L, title, author, isbn, publicationYear);
    }
}
```

Validation lives on the `@Create` constructor parameters (per the cheat sheet), enforcing title ≤ 200 chars and all fields required.

**`src/test/java/com/example/catalog/BookIntegrationTest.java`** — an `@IntegrationTest` covering create→get and the 404 path.

## How the requirements are met (from generated code I inspected)

- **`POST /books`** → `ResponseEntity.created(URI.create("/books/" + id))`: `201 Created` with a `Location` header ending in the new id.
- **`GET /books/{id}`** → returns `BookResponse` (fields `id`, `title`, `author`, `isbn`, `publicationYear`, plus `version`) or `404 Not Found` when absent.
- **PostgreSQL storage** — `prefab-postgres` is on the classpath; the processor generated `target/classes/db/migration/V1__generated.sql` creating the `book` table (`id` PK, `version`, `title`/`author`/`isbn` VARCHAR NOT NULL, `publication_year` INTEGER NOT NULL).

## Verification

- `mvn -DskipTests compile` — clean (only unrelated JDK/guice warnings).
- `mvn -Dtest=BookIntegrationTest test` — 2 passed.
- `mvn verify` (full suite, including Prefab's generated conformance tests) — **BUILD SUCCESS**, 2 tests, 0 failures.

No `target/` files were edited, and no controller/service/repository/entity/migration was hand-written. Nothing is committed, as that wasn't requested.
